title: 'Cache-aware pricing: discount cached_tokens once Langertha::Pricing models
  a cache rate'
updated: 2026-09-25T16:41:23Z
---

cached_tokens is recorded per usage event since k27 (ADR 0013), but cost_*_usd still bills cached tokens at the normal input rate. Correct billing needs Langertha::Pricing->cost_for to model a cache-discount rate (and ideally Langertha::Usage to expose the count so it can be priced from the normalized path instead of the raw payload). Until that lands upstream, Skeid must not invent a discount of its own. Done-when: Langertha::Pricing models a cache rate; Skeid prices cached_tokens at it; a test proves the stored cost reflects the discount. Builds on the recorded count from k27.

